{{Politics of Slovenia}}
Presidential elections were held in [[Slovenia]] on 23 November 1997. The result was a victory for incumbent [[Milan Kučan]], who won 55.54% of the vote. Voter turnout was 68.65%.<ref>[http://eed.nsd.uib.no/webview/index.jsp?study=http://129.177.90.166:80/obj/fStudy/SIPR19921_Display&mode=cube&v=2&cube=http://129.177.90.166:80/obj/fCube/SIPR19921_Display_C1&top=yes Dataset: Slovenia: Presidential Election 1997] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190306015605/http://eed.nsd.uib.no/webview/index.jsp?study=http%3A%2F%2F129.177.90.166%3A80%2Fobj%2FfStudy%2FSIPR19921_Display&mode=cube&v=2&cube=http%3A%2F%2F129.177.90.166%3A80%2Fobj%2FfCube%2FSIPR19921_Display_C1&top=yes |date=6 March 2019 }} European Elections Database</ref>

